nder an open sky  and breathe free air it's the birthplace  of humanity and it's not giving up yet  Mars was settled by some of Earth's best  scientists and engineers they built  cities underground and in domes  developed the best spaceships and  science and soon they decided they  didn't want to serve earth anymore  Mars wanted independence which almost  caused war with earth but then a Martian  called Solomon Epstein invented the  abstain drive a rocket technology that  made spaceships fly far faster and  further than before  Solomon's test drive accelerated so fast  that it killed him and a hundred and  thirty years later you can still see his  ship shooting into deep space the best  longest funeral in history Mars  recovered Epstein's design and shared  the drive with earth in return for  independence  so now Mars has its own government and  military and stands as a rival  superpower to earth but while earth is  bloated and slow Mars is driven and  focused on one goal to terraform Mars to  turn a lifeless Rock into a garden this  shared purpose unites Martians from many  different backgrounds the Mariner Valley  was settled by East Indians Chinese and  Texans so you get Martians like Alex  Kemal who looks Indian but speaks in a  Texan drawl Mars brings together some of  humanity's best and brightest with the  shared goal of transforming the red  planet but Mars as technology and  military makes their rivalry with Earth  dangerous war could bring disaster on  both planets people born in the asteroid  belt are called belters since they grow  up in low gravity belt as a tall and  thin with wake bones some can't even  survive the gravity of Earth they've  become a separate people with their own  culture adapted to space they have their  own language and hand gestures to  communicate through spacesuits in the  show they have special tattoos old  spacesuits used to burn belters necks so  their tattoo to cover the scar now even  unburned belters get the tattoos as  marks of cultural identity these are a  people who ventured into the darkness of  space to explore find fortune and  freedom but the belt is still mostly  controlled by the inner planets Earth  and Mars inner governments and  corporations owned Bell  stations and mines imposing heavy taxes  tariffs and unfair laws some inners a  racist against belters seeing them as no  longer human because of their  differences in response to this  oppression the outer planets alliance or  OPA fights for belter rights but it's a  loose decentralized network that  includes criminal and terrorist elements  OPA leader Fred Johnson tries to unite  and legitimize the OPA  even though Fred was originally a  military leader for Earth at the same  time Fred runs an engineering company  that's building a giant spaceship for  Mormons who want to colonize distant  space so the expanse has all these  different competing factions whose  cultures and conflicts are shaped by the  physics of space like in space there's  almost no gravity which is a problem  because your muscles waste away your  drinks spill everywhere and the VFX goes  over budget a lot of sci-fi shows get  around this by inventing some gravity  plating that magically gives ships  gravity but the expanse is more  realistic because it's spaceships use  acceleration or thrust to make gravity  it's like how accelerating a car pushes  you back in your seat by accelerating  constantly a spaceship can use that push  back as gravity pulling you down towards  the thruster the faster you accelerate  the stronger the gravity so flying at 1g  is earth gravity while two G's is double  earth gravity making you wait Weiss as  much when you're in a hurry or in combat  ships might fly at five or six GS the  expanse has a drug called the juice  which helps people survive this but too  much g-force will kill you an Epstein  ship can accelerate constantly for the  first half of a trip then flip around  and thrust in the other direction to  decelerate f